Appendix 5:


                     Color Codes


What are color codes?

A color code, is a short sequence that you or a user can enter into
a message to change the color of the text, produce bold text or
basically modify the display attributes.  A color code always starts
with a control-P (which can be produced by hitting the Ctrl key and
the P key at the same time), followed by a character.  Those
characters are listed below.

        1 = BLACK (default background color)
        2 = RED
        3 = GREEN
        4 = YELLOW
        5 = BLUE
        6 = MAGENTA
        7 = CYAN
        8 = WHITE (default character color)

Pressing the SHIFT key while doing any of these numbers, will  change
the background color of your characters.

A few more useful color codes:

        0 = Restore all settings back to default.
        9 = Clears the screen.
        - = Go to BOLD mode.
        = = Go to ITALIC mode.
        \ = Go to UNDERLINE mode.



MACRO CODES:

Two key codes produce macros, which can be defined and changed by
the user by using the macro editor (menu function 'Q').
 
        Q = Gives macro one.
        W = Gives macro two.


CUSTOM CHARACTER CODES:

A few color codes listed below, act somewhat like EIC's except that
users are allowed to enter them into messages.
 
        N = Name of the reading user.
        O = Phone number of the reading user.
        S = City and State of the reading user.
        C = Computer owned by the reading user.

Please note that when you use these four codes, you won't see your
name, or other information printed. Instead, the letter will be simply
printed. The reason for this is because it allows you to delete the
code in case you make a mistake. 

Also, plenty of room should be left on a line containing one of those
codes.  If a user has a very long name, it may wrap off the screen and
onto the next line, producing a ragged-looking screen. Leaving the
line halfway filled should be good enough for any of the four codes.

Note:  Any sysop who has been using 4D-BBS for a long while may recall
that there was a color code that printed out a user's password. It has
been removed from 4D-BBS since version 1.50 because this could cause a
possible security problem.  A user's password is NEVER displayed by
4D-BBS except in the local status window.
